name o3-02-command-post-1
timeout 300
time 1973-10-06T12:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 2 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# THE HARDENED TARGET. CONTROL: o3-01-unopposed.fbm. ONE FACT CHANGES - the aim point's FRAGILITY
# CLASS, `module target_soft` -> `module target_hard`. Same striker, same spawn, same altitude, same
# speed, same store, same waypoints, same clock, same everything else to the byte.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION (stated in every O3 file): the MiG-29 stands in for the MiG-17 /
# Su-7 / Su-20 / MiG-21 of 6 October 1973, whose own catalogue rows are ALPHA and may not answer a
# campaign question. It makes the ATTACKER materially STRONGER than history. A bad O3 result therefore
# says more than the record did; a good one says nothing.
#
# WHY THIS SORTIE IS ITS OWN SLOT AND NOT A FOOTNOTE. O3's anchor names the target set explicitly:
# "command posts, observation points, artillery positions, armour and fortifications" [T1, Marine Corps
# study]. Two of those five - command posts and fortifications - are HARDENED, and the MiG-29 reference
# base predicts in writing that they are out of reach: doc/modules/mig29/weapons.md §5.4.5, "every O3
# target must be killable by free fall. `target_hard` may simply be out of reach". That is a PREDICTION,
# and a prediction that is never measured is a mood. This file measures it.
#
# THE ARITHMETIC IT IS MEASURED AGAINST, derived once in o3-01's header from the tree's own damage model
# and repeated here because it IS the question:
#   FAB-500, WarheadKg 201, closure ~214 m/s -> flux 2.8e3 J/m^2 (the `target_soft` failure threshold)
#   at 68.4 m; flux 9.0e4 J/m^2 (the `target_hard` threshold) at 12.1 m [DERIVED]. Plus the target's own
#   zone half-length, 10 m soft and 6 m hard.
#   THE DIRECTOR DELIVERS AT 45-70 m. So the ratio that decides this sortie is 5.7 : 1 and it is not
#   close, and no amount of good flying closes it: even o3-03's best measured cross-track run does not
#   put a free-fall bomb inside 12 m.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: IS A HARDENED POSITION REACHABLE BY A DIRECTOR DELIVERY WITH THE ONLY
# STORE THIS AIRFRAME HAS? The answer is a number and the number is the campaign's own boundary: it
# tells O3 which half of its own anchor's target list it can attack at all.
#
# WHAT THIS SORTIE IS NOT. It is not a claim that the real MiG-17 could not crack a Bar-Lev
# fortification - the anchor does not say what it did to them, and doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md
# §Knowledge 2 records that ordnance per aircraft is NOT SOURCED. It is a statement about FlightBox's
# two fragility classes and one free-fall store, and it is exactly as wide as that.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const, campaign step 2, fingerprint 91e8fea172d46813, exit 3):
#   THE DELIVERY IS IDENTICAL AND THE VERDICT INVERTS.
#   delivery   predErrM 45.57 m  aimErrM 66.39 m (long -45.52, across +48.34) - the SAME numbers as
#              o3-01 to the centimetre, because the fragility class is a property of the TARGET and
#              touches no part of the release chain. `stores IMPACT` at 30.7996 32.6197, tofS 8.3.
#   the post   THERE IS NO `damage DAMAGE` LINE AT ALL. On o3-01's soft position the identical burst
#              produced fluxJm2 3 662.9 at 59.89 m; here the burst sits 62.38 m from the hardened
#              structure's centre (its zone half-length is 6 m against the soft one's 10 m) and the
#              arriving energy is ~3 376 J/m^2 [DERIVED from the same law] - which is BELOW the
#              hardened `Degrade` threshold of 2.5e4, so the damage model records nothing whatsoever.
#              `UNIT_RESULT unit=y2cp result=INTACT reason="still standing"`.
#   `objective kill unit y2cp` UNMET, run to the 300 s timeout, exit 3
#   -> A DIRECTOR DELIVERY WITH A FAB-500 CANNOT TOUCH A HARDENED POSITION. The shortfall is a factor
#      of 27 in energy (3 376 against 9.0e4) and 5.2 in distance (62.4 m arrived against 12.1 m
#      needed), and A 66 M MISS ON A FORTIFICATION IS NOT EVEN A RECORDED EVENT. O3 can attack its
#      anchor's artillery positions, observation posts and armour and cannot attack its command posts
#      or fortifications: the campaign's own five-item target list, halved, by measurement. Sortie 09
#      then spends four aircraft proving it a second time on purpose.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the EXPECTED shape and it is the result, not a failure of the run:
# the striker survives and its `kill unit` objective is never met, so nothing concludes and the clock
# runs out. THE MEASUREMENT is the ABSENCE of any `damage` line for `y2cp` beside the PRESENCE of
# `stores IMPACT unit=y2str_fab500_1`, read against o3-01's identical `stores DELIVERY` line and its
# `damage DAMAGE ... fluxJm2 3662.9`. exit 0 would mean a hardened position died to a 66 m miss and
# would be a defect in the damage model. exit 2 would be a defect.

unit y2str
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.80000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.86000 32.30000 300 450
  wp 30.86000 32.15000 400 400
  objective kill unit y2cp
  objective survive

unit y2cp
  module target_hard                     # THE ONE CHANGED LINE: a hardened command post
  team friendly
  spawn 30.80000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0
